      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 0,
        "impression_count": 16,
        "like_count": 0,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 0,
        "retweet_count": 0
      },
      "text": "Memory Tax, a new paper on arXiv, finds that many dedicated agent memory systems do worse than naive RAG (retrieving chunks straight from the raw history) in many cases, which means building the memory had negative net value there.\n\nThe authors split what memory does per question https://t.co/591uQ0lJkP",
      "url": "https://x.com/thomas_rehmer/status/2115849867364896883"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "2109669786791903233",
